// markdownlint-cli2 config for DRAFT.
//
// Rules below are disabled because they contradict formatting choices
// already deliberate and load-bearing in README.md, CLA.md, and
// CONTRIBUTING.md - not because the project skips linting. This repo
// does not reformat those three files to satisfy a linter; the linter
// is scoped to match them instead.
//
// - MD013 (line-length): FMBOA/BIOPGE reference tables and dense
//   `<details>` blocks routinely exceed 80 chars by design.
// - MD033 (no-inline-html): `<details>`/`<summary>` collapsible
//   sections are the README's primary structuring device throughout.
// - MD060 (table-column-style): README tables are not pipe-aligned;
//   enforcing alignment would force a reformat of existing content.
// - MD028 (no-blanks-blockquote): the `[LICENSE]` SPDX block
//   (`> SPDX-FileCopyrightText: ...`, one blockquote line per field,
//   blank line between each) is the fixed SPDX format used at the end
//   of every DRAFT document - see CONTRIBUTING.md's own template.
// - MD001 (heading-increment): README.md's `a)/b)/c)` intro items are
//   h3 directly under the h1 title, by design (no h2 wrapper wanted
//   for them).
// - MD010 (no-hard-tabs): the workspace-layout code fence in README.md
//   mixes tabs/spaces for alignment inside an already-fenced example;
//   not prose, not worth reformatting.
// - MD012 (no-multiple-blanks): a small number of double blank lines
//   in README.md predate this Makefile and are cosmetic only.
// - MD024 (no-duplicate-heading): BIOPGE blocks in D2/CONCEPTION.md
//   examples legitimately repeat field names ("Process", etc.) across
//   sibling units - that's the format, not a mistake.
// - MD040 (fenced-code-language): a few illustrative fences in README
//   (flag/report templates) are intentionally plain text, not code in
//   any language.
// - MD004 (ul-style): README's `[HORIZON]` closing section uses `*`
//   bullets deliberately, distinct from the `-` used elsewhere.
// - MD041 (first-line-heading): GitHub issue/PR templates start with
//   YAML front matter or form prose, not a top-level heading - GitHub
//   renders them as forms, not as documents.
// MD034 (no-bare-urls) stays enabled globally. AI-skills/ carries its
// own local .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc (markdownlint-cli2's directory-
// level config inheritance) exempting it - see the comment there for
// why: normative method content is not reformatted to satisfy this
// Makefile.
//
// Everything else (broken links syntax, trailing whitespace, etc.)
// stays enabled.
{
  "config": {
    "default": true,
    "MD001": false,
    "MD004": false,
    "MD010": false,
    "MD012": false,
    "MD013": false,
    "MD024": false,
    "MD028": false,
    "MD033": false,
    "MD040": false,
    "MD041": false,
    "MD060": false
  },
  "globs": ["**/*.md"],
  "ignores": ["**/node_modules/**"]
}
